From: Nex package maintainers
Subject: read docutils.conf from the three UAPI system tiers
Source: Nex downstream patch for Docutils 0.21.2
Upstream: not submitted; needs agreement on Unix vendor and transient paths

`OptionParser.standard_config_files` only looked for a system file at
`/etc/docutils.conf`. Extend the list with `/run/docutils.conf` and
`/usr/lib/docutils/docutils.conf` so Nex-built readers honor `/etc`,
`/run`, and `/usr` in that priority, per
`.agents/MANIFESTS_CODE_STYLE.md`.

`get_standard_config_settings` reads every file in
`standard_config_files` in order and lets later files override
earlier ones key by key, so the admin file must sort last among the
three system tiers to win. List order becomes `/usr/lib`, then
`/run`, then `/etc`, keeping the project (`./docutils.conf`) and user
(`~/.docutils`) files last and unchanged. `DOCUTILSCONFIG` still
replaces the whole list when set, matching upstream behavior.

--- a/docutils/frontend.py
+++ b/docutils/frontend.py
@@ -534,7 +534,9 @@
     """

     standard_config_files = [
-        '/etc/docutils.conf',           # system-wide
+        '/usr/lib/docutils/docutils.conf',  # system-wide, package default
+        '/run/docutils.conf',           # system-wide, transient
+        '/etc/docutils.conf',           # system-wide, admin
         './docutils.conf',              # project-specific
         '~/.docutils']                  # user-specific
     """Docutils configuration files, using ConfigParser syntax.
